// Read by every target (ios/project.yml, configFiles). It holds nothing itself: it only takes in
// ios/Private.xcconfig when that file exists. Private.xcconfig is git-ignored and is where an
// organisation keeps its own app identity for its own builds, for example:
//   CMS_BUNDLE_ID = org.example.cms
//   CMS_TEAM = ABCDE12345
//   CMS_DISPLAY_NAME = Example CMS
//   CMS_SPOKEN_NAME = Example Case Management
//   CMS_SIGNIN_TITLE = Example Case Management
//   CMS_DEFAULT_SERVER = cms.example.org
//   CMS_APP_ICON = PrivateAppIcon
// Values set there win over the ones in project.yml. CMS_APP_ICON names an icon set in
// Sources/Assets.xcassets; keep a private one as Sources/Assets.xcassets/PrivateAppIcon.appiconset
// (also git-ignored).
#include? "Private.xcconfig"
